From 1a897a3eb8f7aaa027e9bcec6270c626c65c3fc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:04:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: backport GMU component ownership with safe teardown

Backport the eight-patch GMU sync-state v2 series to this older MSM base.
The GMU must bind a real platform driver so its suppliers can reach
sync_state instead of remaining pending behind an unbound consumer.

Original patches 1-6 are by Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>.
Original patches 7-8 are by Haitao Xu <haitao.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>,
posted by Akhil. This is a combined, adapted backport, not an unchanged
import. Preserve the explicit separate_gpu_kms policy and older GPU
eligibility checks; the newer automatic topology selector is absent here.

Keep private DRM data separate from GPU drvdata, bind GPU and GMU as
components, and initialize devfreq only after both components are ready.
Remove obsolete gpu_ops and migrate every in-tree caller.

Address the applicable v2 review lifetime hazards: reject a missing GMU
before GPU allocation; stop and release all partial preemption resources;
avoid suspension after GMU unbind; remove devfreq before dropping QoS;
and centralize GMU mutex/runtime-PM ownership with balanced bind errors.
The newer MX device link mentioned in review does not exist on this base.

The complete ARM64 MSM object builds with W=1; only the pre-existing
DPU prototype and Y900 PHY format warnings remain. Twenty actual-C
resource/error cases pass; three original unsafe function bodies fail
the same resource oracle. No physical wake or suspend fix is claimed.

Link: https://patchew.org/linux/20261030-gmu-sync-state-fix-v2-0-89d3082d97af@oss.qualcomm.com/
Link: https://lkml.iu.edu/2610.2/03310.html
Link: https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20261030-gmu-sync-state-fix-v2-0-89d3082d97af@oss.qualcomm.com?part=6
